      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To study pre-hospital sudden death so as to reduce the death rate."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHOD",
          "content": "814 pre-hospital deaths were randomly selected from January 1990 to May 1994 for a retrospective study."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "616 deaths (75.7%) showed a history of cardiac disease and hypertension. The age for high sudden death rate ranged from 50 to 69 years (53.9%). Most of the cases (87.8%) were found in their homes. 21 cases (2.58%) successfully recovered."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "The key points to improve the success rate of pre-hospital sudden death are: completing Beijing Emergency Medical Center's emergency care network so as to decrease the emergency care radium and shorten the emergency care time; disseminating emergency care knowledge on CPR and CPR technique."
        }
      ]},
